title: field-audio-tools
---
_template: software.html
---
date: 2026-07-24
---
body:

Two local CLI programs for long Zoom F3 recordings: cut a timestamped excerpt with
provenance, or screen a take in fixed windows for low-frequency dominance.

Requires Python 3.11+, FFmpeg (`ffmpeg`, `ffprobe`) on `PATH`, and NumPy
(installed with the package). Planned license: GPL-3.0-or-later after a stable
public release.

## `soundcite`

<p class="software-tags"><span class="card-type-rs">citation</span><span class="card-type-rs">excerpt</span><span class="card-type-rs">provenance</span><span class="card-type-rs">manifest</span></p>

Extracts a time range and writes lossless excerpts, a listening copy, a
spectrogram, `manifest.json`, and checksums.

<pre class="software-example"><code>soundcite 260115_002_Tr1.WAV 260115_002_Tr2.WAV \
  --start 01:00:00 --duration 20 --output 260115-002-soundcite</code></pre>

## `lowdom`

<p class="software-tags"><span class="card-type-rs">screening</span><span class="card-type-rs">low-frequency</span><span class="card-type-rs">windows</span><span class="card-type-rs">heuristic</span></p>

Scores each short window for low-frequency dominance and writes CSV, JSON, and
static reports. The score is a screening heuristic, not wind probability; water,
handling, and vehicles can look similar.

<pre class="software-example"><code>lowdom 260115_002_Tr1.WAV 260115_002_Tr2.WAV \
  --window 10 --threshold 0.95 --output 260115-002-lowdom</code></pre>

## A test note

Check the first test note on one complete F3 run [here](/software/running-field-audio-tools-on-a-long-f3-take).

A quick view of the results: [soundcite package](/files/software/260115-002-soundcite/index.html) | [lowdom data report](/files/software/260115-002-lowdom/report.html) | [lowdom data report (multimedia)](/files/software/260115-002-lowdom/report-js.html)
